Russell’s Viper bites are known to cause acute pituitary adrenal insufficiency (Tun Pe et al, 1987 ;
Eapen et al 1976). This condition may contribute to shock. Follow-up checks on known Russell’s
Viper victims need to ensure that no long term pituitary sequelae are evident.

